  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "A left Riemann sum is used to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=-1$ and $x=3$ for each of the functions below. For which function does the Riemann sum give an *overestimate* of the area?",
  "worked_solution": "The left Riemann sum overestimates the area under the respective curve if the function is decreasing over the given interval. \n\nOf the given options, the only one that is decreasing over $x\\in [-1,3]$ is the following. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14221930/assets/622f8fd49fb32255b29bd0ae8c36c146aeb4b48aec7be2cde69832cb33fd2d83.png)",
